Question: If I mistakenly take a cash advance with my Horizon credit card instead of using my Horizon savings account, what are the repercussions and how can I avoid any interest charges?

Answer: - Pay the full amount owed right away, covering both the posted balance and any cash‑advance transaction that has not yet appeared on your statement, to prevent interest from accruing. For example:
  • Statement balance as of {{faq_553407fb_001}} May – {{faq_553407fb_002}}
  • Unbilled amount as of {{faq_553407fb_003}} May – {{faq_553407fb_004}}
  • Cash‑advance taken on {{faq_553407fb_005}} May – {{faq_553407fb_006}}
  • Total payment required – {{faq_553407fb_007}}

